UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Knight of Swords represents the absolute archetype of "Systemic Acceleration"—the high-velocity, laser-focused application of intellect that transforms the Page’s observational data into a decisive, unstoppable mission. Moving beyond the data-gathering phase of the Page, the Knight signifies the stage of "The Sovereign Strategist," where you are no longer merely identifying terrain, but charging through it with the force of an absolute, unwavering conviction. Visually depicted as a knight charging forward on a horse with a drawn sword, this archetype embodies the concept of "Sovereign Momentum"—the understanding that true creative agency is found in the ability to commit your entire cognitive capacity to a single, high-priority trajectory. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of "Vector Execution," where your internal processing power is fully focused on a specific, logical conclusion. When the Knight of Swords appears, your system is registering a "Maximum Velocity" status; you have defined your strategy, and you are being invited to stop the "simulation-phase" and fully inhabit the role of the primary driver in your own, logical reality. This card commands you to perform a brutal audit of your resolve. You are being tasked with the essential work of "Intentional Decisiveness": moving past the fear of being "too aggressive," the hesitation of the ego, and the need for nuance where none is required, and committing your full, sovereign authority to the rapid, intellectual advancement of your goal. To inhabit the Knight of Swords is to master the art of "Strategic Speed," recognizing that by engaging in your life with total, uninhibited logical force, you are effectively cutting through the obstacles that previously felt insurmountable, creating a path through the sheer, brute power of your own, intentional mind.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Knight of Swords appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "Systemic Over-acceleration," "Logic-Derailment," or the catastrophic—yet curative—failure of your "full-speed" strategy, leading to a state of total, reckless mental burnout. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates "mental speed" with "intellectual dominance," even as you realize your internal operating system is accelerating toward a collision with reality that you are not prepared to handle. You are essentially "charging off a logical cliff," running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s desire to feel "smarter" and "more aggressive" over the sober, unglamorous requirement to actually navigate the facts. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the "heroic genius," while internally, you are being hollowed out by a profound, gnawing sense of aimless volatility, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency irritability, the experience of "collateral damage from ill-conceived plans," and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your current "rush" is a desperate, ego-driven attempt to outrun your own lack of genuine foundation. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of aggression"; you are obsessively trying to force your logical conclusions onto an environment that is not yet ready, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, tactical slow-down is your own, deep-seated fear that if you were to stop moving, you would have to confront the reality that your "brilliance" is missing the necessary, core components of stability. The reversed Knight of Swords exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of "being slowed down," and the corresponding fear that if you were to drop the frantic pretense of the "conquering intellect," you would be forced to face the reality of your own, present-day, uncoordinated state. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these volatile, high-velocity, aimless scripts, perform a brutal audit of your directional alignment, and confront the reality of why you are so hesitant to prioritize the precision of your movement over the speed of your exit. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance discord, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual authority. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of radical recalibration—accepting that the "stuckness" you feel is the direct result of having prioritized the comfort of "the image of the genius" over the vulnerability of "the truth of the traveler," and realizing that until you are willing to dismount, assess your path, and wait for the true opening, you will continue to be starved by the very, phantom momentum you have worked so hard to simulate.'
WHERE id = 40;
